     "content_html": "<p>Since you are told to assume <span data-math=\"p\"></span> is true and <span data-math=\"q\"></span> is false, you only need one row of possible truth values in your truth table.</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"p\"></span></td>\n<td><span data-math=\"q\"></span></td>\n<td><span data-math=\"{\\text{~}}q\"></span></td>\n<td><span data-math=\"p \\to {\\text{~}}q\"></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>T</td>\n<td>F</td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><span data-math=\"{\\text{~}}q\"></span></p>\n<p>The negation of false is true, so write T under <span data-math=\"{\\text{~}}q\"></span>.</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"p\"></span></td>\n<td><span data-math=\"q\"></span></td>\n<td><span data-math=\"{\\text{~}}q\"></span></td>\n<td><span data-math=\"p \\to {\\text{~}}q\"></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>T</td>\n<td>F</td>\n<td>T</td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><span data-math=\"p \\to {\\text{~}}q\"></span></p>\n<p>The conditional is only false when the hypothesis is true, and the conclusion is false. Using <span data-math=\"p\"></span> and the previous column, you have.</p>\n<p>If True, then True</p>\n<p>The result is True, so write T in the last column.</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"p\"></span></td>\n<td><span data-math=\"q\"></span></td>\n<td><span data-math=\"{\\text{~}}q\"></span></td>\n<td><span data-math=\"p \\to {\\text{~}}q\"></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>T</td>\n<td>F</td>\n<td>T</td>\n<td>T</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n"
